WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.900
In previous videos, you saw us planning to make&nbsp;
our first Level 2 house on the land.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.314
- The Level 2 house doesn't exist yet, 
but just to illustrate&nbsp;what it could look like:

00:00:09.314 --> 00:00:10.952
Something like a shipping container.

00:00:10.952 --> 00:00:14.186
- We went to find trailers to transform&nbsp;into a new home.

00:00:14.186 --> 00:00:18.218
We did a vote with our Patreons,
 because we didn't know which one to choose...

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:21.917
The&nbsp;winner was this old blue pig trailer.

00:00:21.917 --> 00:00:25.910
We installed it in the middle land of Project Kamp,
 which we still&nbsp;don't own...

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.038
It was quite an operation to bring it here!

00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:32.443
Now, it's time to start working on our&nbsp;Level 2 house!

00:00:32.443 --> 00:00:34.680
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.578
Here I am in the Middle Land!

00:00:39.578 --> 00:00:42.030
Finally, we have&nbsp;our big trailer here!

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.227
Ready to be transformed into a new house!

00:00:44.227 --> 00:00:48.132
We are gonna rip it apart to see&nbsp;what is the state of things.

00:00:48.132 --> 00:00:54.668
We then decide what we can reuse, or what not,
 what needs&nbsp;some new work, some welding, some cutting...

00:00:54.668 --> 00:00:55.705
So, let's see!

00:00:55.705 --> 00:00:58.035
Let me show you a bit more in&nbsp;depth what is inside!

00:00:58.035 --> 00:00:59.040
Let's see what is here...

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.028
So, here we are inside the trailer.

00:01:04.028 --> 00:01:06.342
The idea now&nbsp;is to check off:

00:01:06.342 --> 00:01:08.201
''What can we use and what not?''

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.623
''What do we need to take out from here?''

00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:10.628
''What can we use?'' 

00:01:10.628 --> 00:01:12.000
''What do we need&nbsp;to cut?''

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.960
''What can we reuse?''

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.108
''What do we just need to rebuild ourselves?''

00:01:17.108 --> 00:01:21.063
We need to deconstruct the pig trailer first.

00:01:21.063 --> 00:01:23.677
Then, we need to restore it, and then we can start.

00:01:23.677 --> 00:01:25.990
We will start the already&nbsp;with some deconstruction.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.501
Like, we have these bars here...

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:33.900
This is flipped, so they probably reused
this wood already from another different truck.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.060
The state, as you already&nbsp;saw, is a bit how it looks...

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.666
We don't have a roof now.

00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:42.848
It's just tarp.

00:01:42.848 --> 00:01:46.785
It's not&nbsp;really closing properly, because it's completely wobbly.

00:01:46.785 --> 00:01:52.920
This floor used to be wood and metal beams,
but then, someone put this new floor on top.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:58.849
Probably with the animal transport, it began to rot.

00:01:58.849 --> 00:02:02.319
We will see if it's worth to take it apart or not.

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:06.373
Usually, the nuts you can screw out and take it apart.

00:02:06.373 --> 00:02:09.162
That's not the case here...

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.065
Besides the challenges of the trailer itself...

00:02:11.065 --> 00:02:14.820
We also have the&nbsp;challenges of how to 
work here in this environment.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.962
So, we are now in Portugal, and it's summer...

00:02:19.962 --> 00:02:21.873
It's&nbsp;quite hot.

00:02:21.873 --> 00:02:25.952
This comes with some challenges,
 like there's some fire risk around.

00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:29.880
When&nbsp;we work with metal tools, grinders, welding...

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.386
We're also a bit far from the workspace,
 like&nbsp;around 200 meters from Basekamp.

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:37.444
Which also can create some challenges...

00:02:37.444 --> 00:02:39.054
Like, bringing tools up and bringing tools&nbsp;down.

00:02:39.054 --> 00:02:40.920
We don't have battery tools for everything.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:48.292
So, we have these little challenges that we 
will&nbsp;try to tackle as best as we can.

00:02:48.292 --> 00:02:51.812
Also, we have some new people that 
we want to introduce to you!

00:02:51.812 --> 00:02:54.720
Some of them you might already seen somewhere.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.216
Some of them maybe you remember from other&nbsp;times.

00:02:58.216 --> 00:03:00.960
But, let's introduce them properly first!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.648
- Hey! I'm Robert!

00:03:06.648 --> 00:03:09.129
I'm 24 years old, and I come from&nbsp;Iceland.

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:12.022
I enjoy country music and physical work.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.628
I have a background in metalworks, but&nbsp;I also like landscaping!

00:03:16.032 --> 00:03:19.393
I came to the project to test myself in a new environment--

00:03:19.393 --> 00:03:20.648
Fuck! It's hot here!

00:03:20.648 --> 00:03:22.244
And, living in a community.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.639
I've been following the project since 
Season&nbsp;1, and I'm also a Patreon!

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.351
So, it's awesome to experience this firsthand!

00:03:29.351 --> 00:03:35.257
I also really enjoy meat, which is really strange that I'm in a vegan Kamp,
but I have no problem with it!

00:03:35.257 --> 00:03:38.940
And, if I need my things, I can always go to the nearby town and enjoy!

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.949
In the future, I would love to travel&nbsp;to the Southern USA.

00:03:42.949 --> 00:03:45.539
Because, I love the people and the culture there.

00:03:45.539 --> 00:03:48.120
But, for&nbsp;the time being, let's get rid of some rust!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.902
- Hey! I am Wouter!

00:03:53.902 --> 00:03:57.300
I am a designer, maker, and carpenter from the&nbsp;Netherlands!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.616
I love food, music and nature.

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:03.973
Last year, I developed a big interest in&nbsp;sustainable buildings.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:11.393
I hope to find a way of living less consumeristic, 
individualistic, and more close to nature!

00:04:11.393 --> 00:04:14.672
I would love to find a good place for my son to grow up.

00:04:15.211 --> 00:04:18.419
Last&nbsp;year, you could see me building the yoga decks.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.351
This year, I'm designing and building the Level 2 house!

00:04:21.351 --> 00:04:28.500
I'm back at Project Kamp to work on positive change,
and get inspired by&nbsp;a different, but same-minded people!

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.540
- Now that the people are introduced, we can finally start with the project!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.878
First thing to do: bring electricity to&nbsp;the trailer!

00:04:43.459 --> 00:04:46.338
So, we are here: the workshop in Basekamp.

00:04:46.338 --> 00:04:48.400
The pig trailer is here.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.079
We&nbsp;already made a path to the pig trailer to bring it in.

00:04:52.079 --> 00:04:55.332
But, now, we want to make a shorter&nbsp;path for the electricity.

00:04:55.332 --> 00:04:56.640
Okay! Let's start!

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.920
Now you can roll out the cable!

00:05:51.533 --> 00:05:57.408
After we connected the electricity from Basekamp to the trailer,
 our next step is&nbsp;cleaning the area around the trailer

00:05:57.408 --> 00:06:00.668
Reduce the risk of fire during the work.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:14.936
Finally, we can detach the top&nbsp;from the trailer,
 and make a nice shaded area with it.

00:06:14.936 --> 00:06:18.000
A bit sketchy, but for&nbsp;the temporary setting is more than enough!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.440
And then, there was shade!

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.920
It's maybe still a bit sketchy, but it will work.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.057
Look at all this shade!

00:06:44.606 --> 00:06:51.000
- So, now it's time to&nbsp;get rid of the old,
to make room for the new!

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.539
We need to take out the wood panels on the side.

00:06:54.539 --> 00:06:56.940
But, the bolts and nuts are quite rusty...

00:07:01.338 --> 00:07:03.562
We need to find an alternative.

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:13.440
- This was really rusty!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.460
We're cutting off the door!

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:13.800
So, we're gonna do an incision at 
the ground level and then topple this.

00:08:16.384 --> 00:08:17.662
It will come down!

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:38.597
- We took all the screws out of the wall&nbsp;on the back.

00:08:38.597 --> 00:08:39.840
So, we now can tear it down!

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.219
What are you up to, Robert?

00:09:02.219 --> 00:09:07.320
- We're about to cut off the floor with a big ass grinder!

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:12.524
Because, it's really, really rusted,
and about&nbsp;to fall through...

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.406
- Do you think this is rusty?

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.983
We take this one first I think.

00:09:28.983 --> 00:09:31.800
Maybe check if we can lift it up with the bar?

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:37.061
And then, if the floor is loose, we can maybe start on that part?

00:09:37.061 --> 00:09:39.720
Then, we go to this part.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.926
- Sounds good!

00:09:41.926 --> 00:09:42.479
You ready?

00:09:42.479 --> 00:09:43.297
- Yup!

00:09:43.802 --> 00:09:46.705
Let's&nbsp;see what we find underneath!

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:13.800
The reason why we have the sheet here is 
to&nbsp;prevent the sparks from hitting the grass!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.805
So, we don't cause a wildfire or fire...

00:10:17.805 --> 00:10:21.561
Because&nbsp;then all of the beloved neighbors will most likely lose their lands...

00:10:21.561 --> 00:10:27.600
We'll see Project&nbsp;Kamp start from the beginning, or no start at all.

00:10:50.292 --> 00:10:51.831
Come on, Jaime!

00:11:35.516 --> 00:11:38.710
- It seems Robert has some welding to do.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.700
Fuck...

00:11:48.345 --> 00:11:50.385
That was probably a really good shot!

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:06.753
- So, we want to push it this morning,
 and finish&nbsp;all the cutting and the grinding.

00:12:06.753 --> 00:12:11.277
Because, as you can see, it's a cloudy morning and foggy.

00:12:11.277 --> 00:12:17.427
And&nbsp;also, everything is humid, so we can use power&nbsp;tools before 11 AM.

00:12:17.427 --> 00:12:20.831
Also, we are using some precautions.

00:12:20.831 --> 00:12:21.331
We have water here and a fire extinguisher.

00:12:42.357 --> 00:12:43.563
- Why do you do that?

00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:47.880
I'm preventing, so that Robert won't cut through the frame.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:54.540
These Icelandic people are sometimes rough.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:50.694
- You can see the real big beam can carry a lot&nbsp;of weight!

00:13:50.694 --> 00:13:53.797
It goes all the way from the front to the back.

00:13:53.797 --> 00:13:55.260
Then, we have wood.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:59.760
And then, there are some&nbsp;O-shaped beams here,
 that carry the wooden beams.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:06.079
On the edge, you can that the wood is bit rotten.

00:14:06.079 --> 00:14:08.100
There is quite some rust.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.801
I think we need to do something with this...

00:14:11.801 --> 00:14:14.725
For the rest, all seemed quite okay.

00:14:14.725 --> 00:14:18.916
A few bad spots in the middle,
 but we must be able to carry&nbsp;quite some load.

00:14:18.916 --> 00:14:22.015
Here, we have the most rusty bit of the trailer.

00:14:22.015 --> 00:14:24.635
Some really big holes...

00:14:24.635 --> 00:14:26.098
Rotten wood...

00:14:26.637 --> 00:14:28.868
Here is the beam at the bottom on the side.

00:14:28.868 --> 00:14:33.759
It's really the wood next to it that is really bad...

00:14:33.759 --> 00:14:38.639
Also, the steel&nbsp;is pretty rusty,
so we have to take the wood out.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:45.480
To make sure that we can protect&nbsp;this side,
 against any future damage.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.423
- What are we gonna start doing&nbsp;Robert?

00:15:45.423 --> 00:15:52.620
We are cleaning the frame, so we can get most of the paint
 and&nbsp;rust off, just so we can repaint it again.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:41.114
After we cleared the rust, we needed to do a better welding.

00:16:41.114 --> 00:16:46.552
So, we took down the machine and the generator to the trailer, 
because our solar&nbsp;is not enough for welding.

00:16:46.552 --> 00:16:47.280
But then...

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.140
- Hey Robert!

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:53.351
What's up, Javi?

00:16:53.351 --> 00:16:56.856
- Do you know where the welding&nbsp;shots from the pig trailer?

00:16:56.856 --> 00:16:57.480
No?

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:01.487
I think I forgot to take them?

00:17:03.709 --> 00:17:05.167
- The life of a&nbsp;video maker...

00:17:05.167 --> 00:17:08.716
Anyway, you can see the results in the photos they've took.

00:17:08.716 --> 00:17:10.732
They seem&nbsp;sturdy enough!

00:17:10.732 --> 00:17:14.699
Okay, so now, let's take out the backdoors.

00:17:14.699 --> 00:17:21.568
- We want to take&nbsp;these doors out,
but the hinges are connected with one big piece of metal.

00:17:21.568 --> 00:17:24.282
We are going to take it out at once.

00:17:24.282 --> 00:17:31.583
We are gonna cut this hinge here and here,
 and just hammer the upper part out and this one out.

00:17:32.492 --> 00:17:35.409
Hopefully, we can get the door out.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:47.684
Easy!

00:17:47.684 --> 00:17:50.280
The first door is out -- let's go for the second one!

00:18:10.277 --> 00:18:11.649
- The bar is like bended.

00:18:12.167 --> 00:18:15.758
We can&nbsp;cut here, and take this out.

00:18:20.611 --> 00:18:22.151
It's not moving at all...

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.940
It's stuck, and I don't know where it's stuck.

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:18.075
- So, we made a thousand shots.

00:19:18.075 --> 00:19:22.823
We've ran into some&nbsp;issues, but the doors are out!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:33.129
- So, now we're gonna clean the metal, 
degrease&nbsp;it and then paint it.

00:19:33.129 --> 00:19:38.654
Luckily, today, we have some help from General Help: Constance&nbsp;and Alon

00:19:38.654 --> 00:19:40.080
We're gonna get good progress today!

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:55.430
- Chester is working hard as always.

00:20:25.438 --> 00:20:29.628
Okay, so, we just finished prepping the whole frame!

00:20:29.628 --> 00:20:33.223
Thanks Patreon for this amazing experience...

00:20:33.223 --> 00:20:36.291
Now, we can focus on painting the whole thing.

00:20:36.291 --> 00:20:40.461
We found the same color of paint!

00:20:40.461 --> 00:20:44.531
We will see what we do with the floor, after painting&nbsp;everything.

00:20:44.531 --> 00:20:45.727
Still thinking about it...

00:20:45.727 --> 00:20:49.411
Maybe, we redo the whole floor, or we build the floor on it?

00:20:49.411 --> 00:20:53.616
So, yeah, for now, it's painting time!

00:20:54.458 --> 00:20:55.544
- Let's go!

00:20:55.544 --> 00:20:56.269
Let's go!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.578
We're going to start with this side.

00:21:30.578 --> 00:21:32.401
It's a&nbsp;lot of work!

00:21:32.401 --> 00:21:35.100
All these little corners here and bars.

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:55.953
- What are we doing, Jaime?

00:21:58.411 --> 00:22:01.952
Good morning, I got an early start.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:11.940
We are clearing all the rust and pieces&nbsp;
that fell off the trailer on the floor.&nbsp;

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:20.698
And also, we have a bunch of materials here
that&nbsp;we really can't use.

00:22:20.698 --> 00:22:26.389
We have some of them that we can use that we're gonna try
 and make something&nbsp;out of it.

00:22:26.389 --> 00:22:34.291
But, we also have wood that we can't use anymore,
 or metal that's all rusted out.

00:22:34.291 --> 00:22:40.724
I think we have to make a few trips
 to the waste facility and throw it away.

00:22:40.724 --> 00:22:47.894
Then, clear everything under the trailer,
like all the rust and stuff that fell on&nbsp;the floor.

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:35.640
- So, dear camera, we're now going on an adventure&nbsp;
to find a place where we can drop this stuff off.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:51.173
So, somebody told us about this new place
 to&nbsp;get rid of metal.

00:23:51.173 --> 00:23:52.347
It's a cool place!

00:23:52.347 --> 00:23:54.535
They weigh the car when you come in.

00:23:54.535 --> 00:23:58.216
You leave your&nbsp;stuff, and then they weigh the car again.

00:23:59.394 --> 00:24:01.352
They pay you&nbsp;for the metal!

00:24:01.352 --> 00:24:07.034
- So, for 580 kilos of metal, we got 116 euros.

00:24:07.034 --> 00:24:08.012
Not bad!

00:24:08.012 --> 00:24:11.880
We recovered some&nbsp;cash, and now this material will be recycled.

00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:21.600
We had to do a few trips back to the place.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:25.260
But, after that, it was only&nbsp;some wood left to get rid of.

00:24:31.020 --> 00:24:31.980
- Watch out!

00:24:39.420 --> 00:24:43.770
''In 3rd place, we have the trampoline jumper from France: Colleen!''

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:54.235
- We loaded up the pickup and took it to the&nbsp;local waste facility.

00:24:54.235 --> 00:24:56.520
Now, we have the place cleared.

00:25:01.484 --> 00:25:06.270
We need to get some solid materials
 to&nbsp;renovate the trailer, and we need your help to&nbsp;choose.

00:25:06.270 --> 00:25:12.399
So, we went to the scrapyard to search materials,
 and it's actually not easy to find good recycled materials here...

00:25:12.399 --> 00:25:17.232
But, we found this&nbsp;stack of old Trespa,
 used for promotional stands or something.

00:25:17.232 --> 00:25:22.380
It should be sturdy enough for the outside,
 but the colors are a bit intense.

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:25.800
But, hey: you can't always choose when recycling!

00:25:26.520 --> 00:25:30.178
So, we want to use this,
 and we made a few color&nbsp;options to choose from.

00:25:30.178 --> 00:25:35.284
If you support us on Patreon, 
you can vote for which color we should&nbsp;pick.

00:25:35.284 --> 00:25:39.180
Sign up on Patreon to vote,
and we will do whatever comes out of it.

00:25:39.180 --> 00:25:42.798
But, for now, we first need to prepare ourselves for the rebuild!

00:25:42.798 --> 00:25:46.142
- So, we're gonna start with the build of the Level 2 house.

00:25:46.142 --> 00:25:51.098
But, right now, we are bringing all the tools up 
and down every day and working here.

00:25:51.098 --> 00:25:54.536
So, we want to make like&nbsp;a little workstation down there.

00:25:54.536 --> 00:25:58.945
I just came from the sawmill, and bought some chestnut beams.

00:25:58.945 --> 00:26:05.541
I'm gonna&nbsp;make two new horses, to make a new workbench
 to work down there, and just leave the tools down&nbsp;there.

00:26:05.541 --> 00:26:09.406
Just so we won't struggle with bringing 
everything back and forth every day.

00:26:09.406 --> 00:26:15.557
So, yeah, I'm just gonna start&nbsp;processing
 and cutting all the beams to size.

00:26:37.620 --> 00:26:39.102
All the cuts are done.

00:26:39.102 --> 00:26:43.939
So, it's time for this guy again.

00:26:43.939 --> 00:26:45.840
Sometimes I like sanding, but...

00:26:46.680 --> 00:26:50.850
Most of the time is just pain in the ass, and today, 
it is a pain in the ass...

00:26:50.850 --> 00:26:52.680
But, yeah, it's worth it!

00:27:10.020 --> 00:27:12.696
I just finished sanding the inner faces of the horses.

00:27:12.696 --> 00:27:18.747
So, right now, I'm going to put them together,
and then I&nbsp;can sand the front and the back.

00:28:21.343 --> 00:28:30.420
Right here, you can see the difference of sanding and routing,
and not sanding and routing the edges.

00:28:30.420 --> 00:28:33.872
For me, it makes sense to take a bit more&nbsp;time.

00:28:33.872 --> 00:28:36.120
Because, the difference is pretty big.

00:29:41.940 --> 00:29:47.245
Okay, so, they just delivered the two top&nbsp;pieces!

00:29:48.457 --> 00:29:50.297
This is the second one.

00:29:50.297 --> 00:29:52.474
That's some normal multiplex,
 so it's going to be the downside.

00:29:52.912 --> 00:29:59.334
This is&nbsp;a special multiplex for outside with a corrugated face.

00:29:59.334 --> 00:30:03.665
That's gonna prevent everything&nbsp;
from moving around, or at least a bit.

00:30:05.348 --> 00:30:11.087
I'm gonna cut the holes in here to put those&nbsp;in place.

00:30:11.087 --> 00:30:13.980
Then, I will screw them together, I think.

00:31:59.820 --> 00:32:05.740
The last thing I want to do is to cover this&nbsp;exposed edge of plywood.

00:32:05.740 --> 00:32:08.633
Just so that the water can't get into it.

00:32:08.633 --> 00:32:19.920
So, yeah, I'm gonna use a leftover&nbsp;beam of chestnut,
cut it to size, and screw it all around the edges.

00:32:35.738 --> 00:32:36.940
It's a snug fit, so...

00:32:36.940 --> 00:32:39.333
- Yeah, I&nbsp;remember it from last time.

00:33:24.840 --> 00:33:27.671
So, now, the restoring part is ready!

00:33:27.671 --> 00:33:30.108
We have ripped it&nbsp;apart:

00:33:30.108 --> 00:33:31.626
the rotten things away.

00:33:31.626 --> 00:33:34.004
We took the things we are not gonna use.

00:33:34.004 --> 00:33:36.403
We sanded it and we repainted it.

00:33:36.403 --> 00:33:43.563
We&nbsp;have brush cut around to keep it easier to work around,
and also reduce the fire risk we have,&nbsp;when working in such a thing.

00:33:43.563 --> 00:33:45.931
We also build a new working station here!

00:33:45.931 --> 00:33:49.630
We have put the tarp on&nbsp;top to be protected from the weather.

00:33:49.630 --> 00:33:51.645
We brought electricity from Basekamp.

00:33:51.645 --> 00:33:53.432
We brought our tools!

00:33:53.432 --> 00:33:56.050
We&nbsp;built a brand new workbench!

00:33:56.050 --> 00:34:00.595
In the next video, we will show you what a day
looks like in Project Camp,&nbsp;just in one shot!

00:34:00.595 --> 00:34:03.876
If you want to watch it already, you can support us on Patreon!

00:34:03.876 --> 00:34:08.181
Otherwise, you can&nbsp;always make suggestions
 and comments on YouTube.

00:34:08.181 --> 00:34:09.885
That always helps the algorithm too.

00:34:10.323 --> 00:34:12.129
So, that's it!

00:34:12.129 --> 00:34:15.438
See&nbsp;you in the next update!

00:34:20.360 --> 00:34:21.756
- Another one!

